<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ethiopia: Who could bring the warring sides to the negotiation table?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1643b4f18e171f8f5ae2152f5d23a1404612a176581fe421921de8f7eb1e9069</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529--2936c02781db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia might be facing its most complex armed conflict in contempary times. The fragile 2022 peace deal has collapsed. International mediators have failed. How will the country manage to return to normal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Renee Good's family sues Trump admin over fatal ICE shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:591978dbdbafe9a223b45519241e993cc78bbdd8fdafe49fd6b232f93481b530</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/renee-good-s-family-sues-trump-admin-over-fatal-ice-shooting/a-79504836--3b01ab91c959.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/renee-good-s-family-sues-trump-admin-over-fatal-ice-shooting/a-79504836?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The family of Renee Good, one of two US citizens fatally shot by federal immigration agents in Minneapolis in January, has sued President Donald Trump's administration alleging negligence and civil rights violations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North and South Korea trade accusations over landmines that injured three soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8aee5e704dc0ef46080e5e8d1d8a32e570c43da3b76428b60b9e77f9c0cb63ef</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854--57b9ec347358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A mine blast that injured three South Korean soldiers has renewed scrutiny of North Korea's actions along the border and raised questions about its strategic goals.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Zimbabwe tycoon Wicknell Chivayo dies in helicopter crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cc6ba6cf908e8b44471ce5419aac2cf44b13806982124d92be9deef6a327dd7</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-tycoon-wicknell-chivayo-dies-in-helicopter-crash/a-79501691--7a89acb12ffe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-tycoon-wicknell-chivayo-dies-in-helicopter-crash/a-79501691?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zimbabwe's President Emmerson Mnangagwa has confirmed the death of businessman Wicknell Chivayo and his wife in a helicopter crash, calling the high-rollers with a lavish lifestyle "consummately philanthropic."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:142439a167235696e91f7e8e7e28e0adbc949fac57036341c9c8111f3a53cc8b</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual assault cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fuelling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UAE launches Flydubai hijacking and terrorism investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c97a38cb5557acd6a19f4c331d5e7c3f9fc39250e63b9c2db35ec15de872d2fc</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746--17ff1e197de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UAE's chief prosecutor said it's looking at the possibility of "terrorist activity or intent" in the alleged attempted hijacking of a Flydubai commercial flight to Tel Aviv. It says it has jurisdiction in the case.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f39afb862a6d77dfdf64e0d13a8a0f1d789d2c61264d0519c9e1fc0bbb9ee398</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: NGO reports dire camp conditions, says Israel is moving 'Yellow Line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af21b24524077e56d0462ab3bc75d6713645d6fa8761456f66615dffd4541f78</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777--aae790bffc81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Danish Refugee Council alleges that Israel is employing "a policy of protracted displacement" in Gaza. It says the so-called "Yellow Line" is creeping west toward the coast, preventing many from returning home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:830d8a135813e60dc07ac08ce320123f049dffd98e96622d4cf0d78da7c2fffb</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are the Houthis winning against Saudi Arabia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:292f021d259f17ad88ccc039e2dedd1dbbca9ec98551279763f7580e90b9caf6</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476--c9910a2a90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's unclear how the Saudis can defuse the threat presented by the Houthis in next-door Yemen or who they can turn to for help. The US isn't interested, the Europeans are hedging and nobody wants open conflict with Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's nuclear program remains shrouded in mystery as the regime debates ditching non-proliferation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99c54e810542b6321bdccfabccda4a27c4237d5bc5e43ef3dd2efe8f8be1e94e</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197--eb083345c8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's nuclear program is entering a critical phase as Tehran debates dropping out of a nuclear non-proliferation treaty. Satellite images also show activity at known nuclear sites.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
